From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:37:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: iommu: apple,dart: name clock protection
 for host-owned DARTs

On T8132, the hosts of some DARTs power them off and restore them around a
deep sleep: the ACIO NHIs, the tunneled PCIe ports and the external display
coprocessors. They need the same clock protection slice as the internal
display DARTs. Extend the description of apple,clock-protection to them.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 2d77c484f930bc00fabf5d1d3662c0331997464a)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
index bbdbb1be90..3bbbf553c6 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/iommu/apple,dart.yaml
@@ -204,7 +204,9 @@ properties:
       power domain of this DART. Its consumer may power that domain down: the
       DART's streams are then disabled and flushed, and the slice disabled,
       before the domain powers off, and the slice is enabled again when it
-      powers up. Only the J713 internal display DARTs use it.
+      powers up. On the J713 the internal display DARTs use it for their DCP's
+      power-down, and the ACIO, tunneled PCIe and external display DARTs for a
+      deep sleep, in which their hosts save and restore them.
 
   apple,manual-availability:
     type: boolean
